`GetFieldIndex` calls `GetMesg` a second time and then scans the field list. This version looks up the message once and scans `mesg->fields` directly, which removes the duplicate message lookup.

The result is unchanged, assuming `GetFieldIndex` is the standard SDK version. That version returns the first index whose `num` matches, or `FIT_UINT16_INVALID`, which the original code turns into `NULL` via the bounds check.

```cpp
const Profile::FIELD* Profile::GetField(const FIT_UINT16 mesgNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    const MESG *mesg = GetMesg(mesgNum);

    if (mesg == NULL)
        return NULL;

    const FIELD *fields = mesg->fields;
    const FIT_UINT16 n = mesg->numFields;
    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (fields[i].num == fieldNum)
            return &fields[i];
    }

    return NULL;
}
```